        "text": "Established on the `cas-certificate` route, in the geometry family. The condition set is MINIMAL by cardinality among the subsets the search budget decided: the certifier tries the empty set first (61.9 ms, nonzero remainder -- so the theorem is genuinely not unconditional) and then the one-element set (220.2 ms, remainder zero). `geometry.nondegeneracy.abc-not-collinear` is listed in the footprint even though it also appears as a hypothesis of `formal.statement`, deliberately: on this route the footprint is the field a reader scans to see what a proof rests on, and a side condition invisible there is precisely how a mechanised geometry proof comes to be quoted as unconditional. `geometry.rabinowitsch-inverse-specialisation` names the step that turns the polynomial identity into the theorem -- substituting the inverse variable, valid exactly off the degeneracy locus.",
